Package: minios-deploy
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.6), python3-dataclasses (>= 0.8-1minios2) | python3 (>= 3.7), parted, e2fsprogs, dosfstools, btrfs-progs, fdisk, mount, ntfs-3g, minios-native-dracut (= ${binary:Version}) | linux-initramfs-tool, openssl | whois, python3-minios-security (>= 1.0.1), udev | eudev, util-linux (>= 2.31)
Recommends: minios-live-config (>= 11.0.5.15), user-setup
Breaks: minios-installer (<< 3.1.0)
Replaces: minios-installer (<< 3.1.0)
Description: command-line MiniOS deployment backend
 minios-deploy provides disk discovery, installation planning, and live or
 native MiniOS deployment without a graphical interface. It is the backend
 used by MiniOS Installer and can also be used directly for automation.

Package: minios-native-dracut
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dracut-core
Provides: linux-initramfs-tool
Conflicts: dracut, initramfs-tools
Description: native initramfs integration for MiniOS
 minios-native-dracut keeps dracut-core available on images that use either
 dracut-mos or livekit-mos and provides native kernel update hooks. The hooks
 are inactive in the live system and are enabled only after a full install.

Package: minios-installer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, minios-deploy (= ${binary:Version}), polkitd | policykit-1, pkexec | policykit-1, python3 (>= 3.6), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-pango-1.0, gir1.2-udisks-2.0, python3-minios-gui (>= 1.4.0), python3-minios-security (>= 1.0.1)
Description: graphical MiniOS installation utility
 MiniOS Installer is the GTK frontend for minios-deploy. It provides guided
 live and native installation workflows while the deployment engine remains
 usable independently from graphical environments.
